BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:Arts
CATEGORIES:Academic/Educational
CATEGORIES:Cultural
CATEGORIES:Social
CATEGORIES:Workshop
CATEGORIES:Drop By
CATEGORIES:Casual/ Relaxed
DESCRIPTION:Step into a world of creativity\, movement and shared ideas at
  Express Yourself!\, a vibrant day of arts\, culture and creative explora
 tion taking place on Saturday\, May 9\, in partnership with the Montclair
  Literary Festival. Open to students\, faculty and the wider community\, 
 this celebration invites everyone to explore creative expression in many 
 forms.\nJoin us for hands-on workshops and interactive experiences on Sat
 urday\, May 9\, 2026. All events are open to all and free\, but registrat
 ion is required. Sign up for a single workshop or all six!\nRegister to A
 ttend\nActing Out: Improv Group Style9 -10:15 a.m.\, Life Hall room 1200C
 rowd Source Acting is about using improvisation to act in the moment. Par
 ticipants will be guided in an improvisational game that allows them to e
 xperience dropping into a roll and having the inspiration of those around
  them to achieve a common goal. That goal could be silly\, serious\, or a
 bsurd. Join us for a round or two of a game called Family Portraits\, gui
 ded by Theatre department practitioners.\nA Moving Experience For All10:3
 0-11:45 a.m.\, Life Hall 1210This session will be a dance class for begin
 ners\, emphasizing freedom of movement and some basic dance moves.\nGot A
 rt? Take This Workshop12:00-1:15 p.m.\, Calcia Hall 245Participants will 
 explore a visual arts technique such as collage\, clay sculpting\, or mix
 ed media and create a unique work. Guided by an artist educator\, attende
 es will learn simple methods and experiment with materials during the ses
 sion.\nSnap Snap: Taking Just the Right Picture1:30-2:45 p.m.\, Feliciano
  School of Business LawnThis digital photography workshop will start with
  a presentation on the powerful choices available for capturing and docum
 enting the world with your camera. Each participant will be given directi
 ons for taking a photograph from a specific location on campus. Jenelle C
 ovino\, Adjunct Professor of Art and Design\, will guide participants to 
 utilize basic photo retouching principles to bring each digital photograp
 h to life. You can bring your digital camera or use your cell phone to ph
 otograph for this workshop. This workshop is suitable for all ages and al
 l experience levels of photography.\nDrumming Up a Crowd\, the West Afric
 an Way3:00-4:15 p.m.\; Feliciano School of Business LawnThe Montclair Sta
 te University West African Drumming and Dance Ensemble will perform and e
 ngage everyone to participate in traditional West African recreational mu
 sic. We play a strong weave of polyrhythms on traditional drums\, bells a
 nd rattles\, and those in attendance will drum with us\, sing with us in 
 call and response in a West African language\, and dance traditional move
 ments with us\, directed by calls from the lead drum.\nLet’s Get Physical
 : Writing Poetry about Memory and the Body4:30-5:45 p.m. Feliciano School
  of Business Room 140In this generative poetry workshop\, we will begin b
 y bringing our memories to life on the page. We will then expand to writi
 ng about embodied experiences. Participants will leave this workshop havi
 ng written two new poems and having received feedback on one of the poems
 . They will also leave with a few additional tools in their writers’ tool
 box.\n\nHosted by: College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS)\n\nAd
 ditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/en
 gage/event/12434336
DTEND:20260509T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260501T040712Z
DTSTART:20260509T130000Z
LOCATION:Locations Across Campus
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Express Yourself! A Day of Creativity\, Community and Discovery
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12434336
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12434336
X-HOSTS:College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS)
